.vercel
# `.claude/` is local-agent state (settings.local.json, caches) EXCEPT the
# skills subtree, output styles, shared settings, hooks, and agent definitions,
# which are team tooling and belong in the repo. A blanket `.claude` can't be
# re-included by a later `!` rule — git never descends into an excluded
# directory — so this must exclude the CONTENTS and re-include.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/output-styles/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
# Agent definitions are shared one file at a time, the way settings.json is:
# re-include the directory so git descends into it, exclude its contents, then
# name the definitions that are team tooling. A contributor's own scratch or
# experimental agents stay local, as everything else under `.claude/` does.
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/reviewer-opus-4-6.md
!.claude/agents/reviewer-opus-5.md
# Driver runtime artifacts: chosen ports + the Chromium profile it drives with.
.claude/skills/*/.state.json
.claude/skills/*/.chrome-profile/
.spark
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/out/

# npm workspaces: only the root lockfile is authoritative. Ignore stray
# per-package lockfiles created by running `npm install` inside a workspace.
**/package-lock.json
!/package-lock.json

# Vite writes a transient timestamped copy of a config next to it whenever the
# config is a TS module; these accumulate and are never source.
**/*.timestamp-*.mjs
